Z||000000||Adrift||09-22-2001||12:28 AM||||A strange question: My key is in the ignition, and it won't come out! I also can't start the engine - I can only turn the key once, but this has no effect. Any idea whats going on?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||09-22-2001||12:30 AM||||What year/model/tranny do you have?  Is your steering wheel locked too?  If you have an auto, be sure it's locked/clicked into park.  If you have an '84... are you depressing the key-release on the column.  If your wheel is locked, does putting turning pressure either way make a difference?  Just some suggestions.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||09-22-2001||12:35 AM||||its an 84 chasis but has all the electronics / engine / etc. out of an 86.<BR>The steering wheel isn't locked. It's a 4spd manual transmission. Another strange thing is you don't have to hit the clutch to change gears, you can just shift.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Adrift (edited 09-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hank is Here||09-22-2001||12:44 AM||||sounds like new ignition time.  how many keys  you got on there?   the more keys the more year on the key and pins which won't make it line up.  Say F it for the night, spray the lock with some lube smack it a few time and come back in the morning hoping for the best.   <P>Hank ||||reg||1
Z||000004||c m west||09-22-2001||01:55 AM||||Don't force it - just get a bigger hammer =-)||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-22-2001||02:21 PM||||could be the lock, the gears/linkage, or the switch itself. Sound more like lock or gears/linkage.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
